<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Metacom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1638–<a href="/years/1676">1676</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Metacomet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Metacom, also called Metacomet and known to the English as King Philip, was a sachem of the Wampanoag and a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massasoit">Massasoit</a>. He succeeded his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wamsutta">Wamsutta</a> in 1662 and faced growing pressure from English settlers on Wampanoag land. In 1675 he led a coalition of Native peoples against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> colonies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-philips-war">King Philip's War</a>, and he was killed in August 1676 near Mount Hope in Rhode Island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/metacom.jpg" alt="Metacom" width="320" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paul Revere · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philip_King_of_Mount_Hope_by_Paul_Revere_(cropped).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
